    "text": "China now accounts for roughly one-third of global physical gold demand, according to the report, making the country one of the most important forces in the bullion market. BMO says sustained buying from China has helped keep gold above $4,000 per ounce, even during periods when investment demand in North America and Europe has been relatively weak. This suggests that Chinese physical demand is becoming increasingly important in supporting the global gold price.",
